6.1 Chosen policy:
Snapshot - Both FullCatalogIterator and PendingStageIterator capture the set of objects they will visit at the moment they are constructed. 
- Structural changes (add / remove / move of a WorkComponent) that occur after an iterator has been created do not appear in that iterator.
- State changes on already-captured objects are visible when the object is later queried (because we store pointers, not deep copies of state), but the membership of the iteration is fixed.
- This matches the common use-case of generating a report or a work-queue view that must remain stable for the duration of the processing run.

